          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Speed comes from facts",
          "body": "Speed is not rushing. It comes from knowing facts by heart (bonds, squares, times tables) and seeing the pattern straight away. Every sprint question uses a pattern from this course."
        },
        {
          "kind": "worked-example",
          "title": "Worked example: three quick ones",
          "problem": "Work out $1000 - 637$, $45^2$ and $25\\%$ of $96$.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "text": "All from $9$, the last from $10$.",
              "try": {
                "prompt": "What is $1000 - 637$?",
                "accepted": ["363"],
                "compute": "1000-637"
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "$4 \\times 5 = 20$, then $25$.",
              "try": {
                "prompt": "What is $45^2$?",
                "accepted": ["2025"],
                "compute": "45^2"
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "Halve twice: $48$, $24$. So $25\\%$ of $96$ is $24$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Accuracy first",
          "body": "If you make a mistake, slow down a little for the next few questions. Getting them all right at a steady pace beats getting half wrong in a rush."
        }
